526	     1	# Recorded responses for the stub model
527	     2	
528	     3	These files are **hand-written**, not captured from a real model. Each one is the answer we expect a model
529	     4	to give under contract `triage.v1` for one of the six messages Dawn forwarded (`docs/input/client-input.md`,
530	     5	section 2.2).
531	     6	
532	     7	- `text` is the message exactly as a tenant sent it. `StubTriageModel` matches a request by the SHA-256 of
533	     8	  the whitespace-trimmed text, so it must stay byte-for-byte identical to the message.
534	     9	- `response` is returned to the pipeline unvalidated and goes through the same `TriageValidator` as a real
535	    10	  model's output would. A string `response` is returned as is, for recording malformed output.
536	    11	
537	    12	Any other message gets the failure `no-recorded-response`, and its job stays Unsure.
